keeps-its-own = Each palette draws each accent in its own tones, and the ringed swatch is whichever one the palette was built around.
language-note = A language chosen here is spoken from the next start.
its-own = Whichever accent this palette was built around
follow-scheme-note = A palette with a light or dark counterpart is worn as the one the desktop asks for; choosing a palette below wears that palette alone.
follow-text-size-note = The nearest of the sizes below to the desktop's own text scale; choosing a size below wears that size alone, and it is the one worn when the desktop does not say.
window-buttons-note = A button the compositor does not offer is left out whatever this says, and a window the compositor draws a titlebar for carries that titlebar's buttons rather than these.
follow-the-system = Follow the system
the-first-language-the-system-lists = The first language the system lists that Resonate speaks, else English.
spoken-whatever-language-the-system-lists = Spoken whatever language the system lists.
always = Always
while-scrolling = While scrolling
never = Never
every-list-and-pane-that-scrolls = Every list and pane that scrolls draws a bar down its edge that shows where the view stands and can be dragged.
a-bar-is-drawn-while-its = A bar is drawn while its list is scrolling and for a moment after, and whenever the pointer is over the edge it sits on, so it can still be taken hold of.
no-bar-is-drawn-a-list = No bar is drawn; a list still scrolls with the wheel and the keys.
flat = Flat
n-3-db-an-octave = 3 dB an octave
n-4-5-db-an-octave = 4.5 dB an octave
each-band-is-drawn-at-the = Each band is drawn at the level it reads: white noise stands level, and music slopes down into the treble.
the-treble-is-lifted-3-db = The treble is lifted 3 dB an octave about 1 kHz, so pink noise stands level and a mastered record does not slope away.
the-treble-is-lifted-4-5 = The treble is lifted 4.5 dB an octave about 1 kHz, the slope a mastered record tends to fall by, so it stands nearer level.
n-60-db = −60 dB
n-78-db = −78 dB
n-96-db = −96 dB
thirds = Thirds
sixths = Sixths
twelfths = Twelfths
slowly = Slowly
middling = Middling
quickly = Quickly
follow-the-desktops-light-or-dark = Follow the desktop's light or dark setting
wear-the-light-or-dark-counterpart = Wear the light or dark counterpart of the palette as the desktop asks
theme = Theme
accent = Accent
follow-the-desktops-text-size = Follow the desktop's text size
draw-the-text-at-the-size = Draw the text at the size nearest the desktop's own text scale
text-size = Text size
reduce-motion = Reduce motion
things-appear-at-once-instead-of = Things appear at once instead of sliding, fading or gliding into place
show-the-minimise-button = Show the minimise button
off-the-window-is-put-away = Off, the window is put away only by the compositor's own gesture
show-the-maximise-button = Show the maximise button
off-a-double-press-on-the = Off, a double press on the titlebar still fills the screen
turn-the-volume-with-the-wheel = Turn the volume with the wheel
over-the-volume-slider-each-notch = Over the volume slider, each notch moves it five per cent
draw-scrollbars = Draw scrollbars
speak = Speak
use-the-mouse-back-and-forward = Use the mouse back and forward buttons
move-through-the-album-and-artist = Move through the album and artist pages opened in this window
show-suggestions = Show Suggestions
the-lists-the-catalog-offers-to = The lists the catalog offers to make out of what it holds
show-missing = Show Missing
what-the-releases-are-short-of = What the releases are short of, and what the artists put out elsewhere
show-the-counts = Show the counts
the-figure-beside-each-tab-how = The figure beside each tab: how many albums, tracks, plays and the rest
treble-lifted = Treble lifted
floor = Floor
bands-an-octave = Bands an octave
bars-fall = Bars fall
remember-the-last-tab = Remember the last tab
off-the-window-opens-on-tracks = Off, the window opens on Tracks
remember-the-window-size = Remember the window size
off-the-window-opens-at-its = Off, the window opens at its built-in size
remember-the-settings-category = Remember the Settings category
off-settings-opens-on-output = Off, Settings opens on Output
text-size-meaning = Everything that holds text — the type, the rows, the sidebar and every control — is drawn at { $percent }% of the middling size.
floor-meaning = A band quieter than { $floor } dB rests on the floor; the plot runs from there to full scale.
bands-meaning = Each octave is cut into { $bands } bands, every band its loudest bin.
falls-meaning = A bar falls { $falls } dB a second once its band quietens; its held peak lets go at half that.
